menu "Feedback (buzzer and RGB LED)"

    config FEEDBACK_BUZZER_GPIO
        int "Buzzer GPIO (-1 = none)"
        range -1 48
        default -1
        help
            Active buzzer (it beeps by itself when powered), on when the
            GPIO is high. Drive it through a transistor if it needs more
            than about 20 mA. GPIO 14 is free on the default pin map.

    config FEEDBACK_RGB_LED_GPIO
        int "RGB LED (WS2812) GPIO (-1 = none)"
        range -1 48
        default -1
        help
            Data pin of one addressable RGB LED (WS2812). The LED on the
            ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1 is on GPIO 48 or 38, depending on the board
            version: check the silkscreen. GPIO 21 is free on the default
            pin map for an external one.

endmenu
